From: Chromium-HaikuOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] content, chrome, services: Haiku fixes for the browser build

- content/browser/file_system_access/file_path_watcher: Haiku has
  neither the inotify nor the kqueue watcher; provide the same no-op
  backend as file_path_watcher_stub.cc (Watch() reports failure).
- content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc: no
  RLIMIT_NPROC; report an unknown process limit.
- content/services/isolated_xr_device, services/network sandbox hooks,
  sandbox/policy/mojom/sandbox.mojom: use the shared BSD sandbox
  declarations, and give Haiku the kVideoCapture sandbox type.
- sandbox/linux/services/proc_util.cc: Haiku's struct dirent has no
  d_type.
- chrome/browser/about_flags.cc: no "audio-backend" flag on Haiku (it
  selects between sndio and PulseAudio).
- chrome/browser/notifications/notification_platform_bridge_linux.cc:
  skip the icon-bytes path that needs memfd (MFD_CLOEXEC).
- components/crash: crashpad's handler is not available on Haiku.
- components/device_signals: LLADDR() returns a different pointer type.
- components/update_client: "haiku" as the OS name.
- services/device/usb: no USB backend on Haiku yet.
- third_party/blink: Haiku links executables as shared objects (-shared),
  where the local-exec TLS model cannot be linked (R_X86_64_TPOFF32); use
  local-dynamic for Blink's heap TLS, as Android does. Stack bounds come
  from pthread_getattr_np(), as on Linux and FreeBSD.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc b/chrome/browser/about_flags.cc
